WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.631
Maddy: Whenever you have a group of people
working together, sooner or later there will

00:00:03.631 --> 00:00:08.871
be some form of conflict that will have to
be resolved, even if it’s only minor issues.

00:00:09.231 --> 00:00:13.761
So, in this video we are going to be
discussing how important it is that a

00:00:13.761 --> 00:00:18.171
manager promotes a positive atmosphere to
minimise the adverse effects of conflict.

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:22.351
Phillip: Although conflict is inevitable,
steps can be taken to help prevent

00:00:22.391 --> 00:00:24.191
conflicts from emerging in the first place.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:29.271
If you do this, you can save time,
energy and resources that would otherwise

00:00:29.271 --> 00:00:33.231
be spent minimising and resolving the
conflict once it’s already broken out.

00:00:34.221 --> 00:00:37.721
Maddy: One of the best things you can do
to make conflicts less likely to occur,

00:00:38.051 --> 00:00:42.741
and less harmful when they do occur, is to
create a positive atmosphere in the workplace

00:00:43.661 --> 00:00:48.941
A negative workplace atmosphere can often be
a consequence of an unresolved conflict or

00:00:48.941 --> 00:00:51.921
conflicts causing people to have lower morale.

00:00:52.851 --> 00:00:56.841
This can in turn lead to the change of
future conflict becoming more likely.

00:00:57.651 --> 00:01:02.941
Employees won’t be as enthusiastic about work
and will be less willing to find solutions

00:01:02.941 --> 00:01:04.521
to their problems with their colleagues.

00:01:05.261 --> 00:01:08.411
With a positive workplace
atmosphere, things are different.

00:01:08.681 --> 00:01:13.501
Morale is higher, people will feel happier
and more energised, more enthusiastic

00:01:13.511 --> 00:01:16.191
about work, and often more valued.

00:01:16.741 --> 00:01:21.351
It also minimises the chances of conflicts
occurring, as people will be more open with

00:01:21.351 --> 00:01:23.671
each other and more focused on their jobs.

00:01:24.341 --> 00:01:29.181
So, what steps can be taken to
promote a positive atmosphere at work?

00:01:30.181 --> 00:01:31.991
Phillip: Arrange Social Events and Mixers

00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:36.591
This will encourage people in the team
to unwind and let off some steam, helping

00:01:36.591 --> 00:01:38.331
to make them more relaxed and happier.

00:01:39.101 --> 00:01:43.261
More importantly, it can also encourage
members of a team to learn more about

00:01:43.301 --> 00:01:45.401
each other, outside of the work context.

00:01:46.041 --> 00:01:50.281
This can help form friendships and
improve interpersonal relationships,

00:01:50.341 --> 00:01:54.631
helping them see each other as real
people instead of just work colleagues.

00:01:55.391 --> 00:01:56.621
Maddy: Team Building Activities

00:01:57.231 --> 00:02:01.541
Time and budget permitting, running team
building activities like workshops and away

00:02:01.541 --> 00:02:07.241
days can help put people together in alternate
situations and encourage them to solve problems.

00:02:07.781 --> 00:02:12.241
By putting them in an environment which is not
work related and they have the opportunity to

00:02:12.241 --> 00:02:17.411
safely fail and people can learn more about
each other and learn to trust each other more.

00:02:18.181 --> 00:02:22.851
It also creates a shared experience and
memory that they can refer back to later.

00:02:23.991 --> 00:02:25.191
Phillip: Get to Know Your Team

00:02:25.861 --> 00:02:30.651
As a team leader, it’s important to spend time and
make the effort to get to know your team better.

00:02:31.711 --> 00:02:35.121
This can help to make you more approachable
to them and help break down the

00:02:35.131 --> 00:02:38.841
barriers that can make the relationship
between you and your team impersonal.

00:02:39.811 --> 00:02:44.651
If the relationship is friendlier and warmer, the
general attitude of your team will be improved.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:47.901
Maddy: Encourage Collaboration in the Team

00:02:48.451 --> 00:02:52.941
Impress on your team how important it is for
everyone to work together and collaborate.

00:02:53.611 --> 00:02:58.221
This will help encourage the team to think
of itself as unified, rather than as divided.

00:02:58.831 --> 00:03:04.031
You can do this with a communications campaign,
which can be as simple as emails and posters,

00:03:04.481 --> 00:03:09.331
or involve workshops and presentations,
whatever works best for you and your team.

00:03:10.051 --> 00:03:11.521
Phillip: Be available to your team

00:03:11.571 --> 00:03:15.821
Make sure your team knows you are accessible
and how to reach you if they need to.

00:03:16.371 --> 00:03:18.961
Proactively check in with
people to see how they’re doing.

00:03:20.001 --> 00:03:23.621
Ask questions and be there to answer
questions that are posed to you.

00:03:24.341 --> 00:03:28.611
This will make your team feel like they can
rely on you and make it more likely that they’ll

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:33.681
come to you first if a conflict is starting to
develop, so you can help to nip it in the bud.

00:03:34.621 --> 00:03:38.961
Maddy: Remember being a manager or team
leader puts you in a good position to

00:03:38.961 --> 00:03:42.911
promote a positive atmosphere when guiding
your team and to so come on, take on

00:03:42.911 --> 00:03:44.991
board what we have said and give it a go.

